# Automatic plots: autoplot

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

ggplot2's reference page for [`autoplot()`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/autoplot.html)
has no examples, so this notebook says only what the page describes and where Giggly stands.

`autoplot()` makes a complete ggplot2 plot for an object of a particular class in a single call,
the class deciding which plot. ggplot2 defines it as an S3 generic, and other packages write
methods for their own classes, as ggplot2's `automatic_plotting` page describes. Not in Giggly
yet: `autoplot()`.
